lute and percentage differences. I'll use the standard adjustment formula to ensure accuracy in my computation.\n\nThe final result shows the adjusted values and percentage differences. I've carefully rounded the absolute difference to the nearest whole number and the percentage difference to three decimal places, ensuring precision in the financial analysis.\n","signature":""},{"type":"toolRequest","id":"call_68ea44d285ea4d6fa764ccf4","toolCall":{"status":"success","value":{"name":"shell","arguments":{"command":"python3 -c \"\n# Raw values (in millions) - from Treasury Bulletin data\nnov_1949_raw = 155205\ndec_1949_raw = 154962\n\n# CPI-U (not seasonally adjusted) - historical values from BLS\ncpi_nov = 121.5\ncpi_dec = 121.2\n\n# Adjust November 1949 to constant December 1949 dollars\nnov_1949_adj = nov_1949_raw * (cpi_dec / cpi_nov)\ndec_1949_adj = dec_1949_raw  # Already in December 1949 dollars\n\nprint(f'November 1949 (adjusted to Dec 1949 dollars): {nov_1949_adj:.6f} million')\nprint(f'December 1949 (in Dec 1949 dollars): {dec_1949_adj:.6f} million')\n\n# Absolute difference (rounded to nearest whole number)\nabs_diff = abs(dec_1949_adj - nov_1949_adj)\nprint(f'\\\\nAbsolute difference: {abs_diff:.6f}')\nprint(f'Absolute difference rounded to nearest whole: {round(abs_diff)}')\n\n# Absolute percentage difference \n# Using the November adjusted value as the base for percentage calculation\nabs_pct_diff = abs((dec_1949_adj - nov_1949_adj) / nov_1949_adj) * 100\nprint(f'\\\\nAbsolute percentage difference: {abs_pct_diff:.6f}%')\nprint(f'Absolute percentage difference rounded to 3 decimal places: {round(abs_pct_diff, 3)}')\n\n# Output format [absolute percentage difference, absolute difference]\nprint(f'\\\\nFinal answer: [{round(abs_pct_diff, 3)}, {round(abs_diff)}]')\n\""}}},"_meta":{"goose_extension":"developer"}}],"metadata":{"userVisible":true,"agentVisible":true}}}
