9's price level. Using the CPI ratio of 121.2/121.5, I'll adjust November's original amount of 155,205 million to reflect December 1949's economic conditions. This yields 154,821.78 million in constant dollars, providing a precise comparison between the two months.\n\nDecember's actual value remains 154,962 million in current dollars, which is appropriate since it's already expressed in December 1949's price level. This method ensures accurate dollar-value comparisons across different time periods.\n","signature":""},{"type":"toolRequest","id":"call_303dfd48116bea52","toolCall":{"status":"success","value":{"name":"shell","arguments":{"command":"python3 -c \"\n# Both values adjusted to constant December 1949 dollars\n\n# Raw values (in millions)\nnov_1949_raw = 155205\ndec_1949_raw = 154962\n\n# CPI-U (not seasonally adjusted)\ncpi_nov = 121.5\ncpi_dec = 121.2\n\n# Adjust both to constant December 1949 dollars\n# November adjusted: multiply by (Dec CPI / Nov CPI)\nnov_in_dec_dollars = nov_1949_raw * (cpi_dec / cpi_nov)\n\n# December is already in December dollars (CPI ratio = 121.2/121.2 = 1)\ndec_in_dec_dollars = dec_1949_raw * (cpi_dec / cpi_dec)\n\nprint('=== Both values in constant December 1949 dollars ===')\nprint(f'November 1949 in Dec 1949 dollars: {nov_in_dec_dollars:.6f} million')\nprint(f'December 1949 in Dec 1949 dollars: {dec_in_dec_dollars:.6f} million')\n\n# Calculate absolute difference\nabs_diff = abs(dec_in_dec_dollars - nov_in_dec_dollars)\nprint(f'\\\\nAbsolute difference: {abs_diff:.6f} million')\nprint(f'Absolute difference (rounded to nearest whole): {round(abs_diff)}')\n\n# Calculate absolute percentage difference\nabs_pct_diff = abs((dec_in_dec_dollars - nov_in_dec_dollars) / nov_in_dec_dollars) * 100\nprint(f'\\\\nAbsolute percentage difference: {abs_pct_diff:.6f}%')\nprint(f'Absolute percentage difference (rounded to 3 decimal places): {round(abs_pct_diff, 3)}')\n\nprint(f'\\\\nFinal answer: [{round(abs_pct_diff, 3)}, {round(abs_diff)}]')\n